    "field": "Shallow cumulus cloud feedbacks",
    "problem": "Climate models exhibit a large spread in climate sensitivity estimates because they fundamentally differ in how they represent key processes, like convective mixing, that control shallow cumulus cloud feedbacks in the trade-wind regions.",
    "method": "This paper is a review that synthesizes current understanding of trade-wind shallow cumulus cloud feedbacks from models and observations; it does not propose a new method to solve a problem.",
    "task": "The task is to review the physical mechanisms controlling trade-wind shallow cumulus cloud feedbacks to understand the diversity of model responses and its impact on climate sensitivity estimates.",
